1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,060
Slide 25 breaks down REAL-TIME SCREEN TRANSLATION: Preserving Visual Harmony.

2
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:09,802
Look at how advanced this pipeline is, students!

3
00:00:09,802 --> 00:00:13,492
It doesn't just pop up a boring text translation box.

4
00:00:13,492 --> 00:00:17,810
It performs in-place pixel inpainting directly on your screen!

5
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:26,830
Step 1: The Frame Difference Detector monitors screen changes, ignoring static wallpaper and processing only active window text.

6
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:36,110
Step 2: Neural Inpainting erases foreign language characters (like Japanese or German) and seamlessly restores the background texture behind the letters!

7
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:47,170
And Step 3: DirectWrite matches the original font's exact size, weight, color, and drop-shadow, rendering the English translation directly over the original image!

8
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:55,730
You look at a Japanese engineering blueprint or German medical manual, and it appears seamlessly in English as if it were originally printed that way!

9
00:00:56,130 --> 00:01:02,180
Eliminating language friction through visual inpainting expands the global reach of human knowledge.

